Body:
The code patch you provided seems to be modifying a Gradle build configuration file. Here are some observations and suggestions for improvement:

1. The change in the `dependencies` block of the `buildscript` section updates the classpath of the Android Gradle Plugin from version `7.3.1` to `8.1.4`. This could potentially introduce compatibility issues with other dependencies or plugins. Make sure to check the release notes and documentation for any breaking changes or migration steps associated with the newer version.

2. It appears that there is a duplication in the `dependencies` block. The `dependencies { }` block is nested within another `dependencies { }` block. You can remove the inner block to fix this issue.

Here's the revised code patch:

```
buildscript {
   repositories { google() }
   dependencies { classpath("com.android.tools.build:gradle:8.1.4") }
}

plugins {
    // Other plugin configurations...
}
```

Remember to thoroughly test your project after applying the changes to ensure everything works as expected, especially if there are additional parts to the build configuration beyond what you've shared.

